      "accepted_answers": null,
      "value_tolerance": 0,
      "question_type": "mcq",
      "rationale": "Design-Bid-Build separates design and construction into sequential phases. The architect completes design, then contractors bid for construction work, maintaining clear separation of responsibilities. SPP 206. [A]: Sequential separation is DBB's defining characteristic. [C]: That describes CM-at-Risk, not DBB. [D]: That describes IPD, not DBB.",
